.TH REAC-STAGEBOXES 1 "" "reac-stageboxes" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reac-stageboxes \- set phantom power, pad and sensitivity on REAC stagebox inputs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reac-stageboxes
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GTK4/libadwaita application that shows every REAC segment in the PipeWire
graph and sets phantom power, the pad and the sensitivity of each input of the
selected stagebox.
It is a PipeWire client: it reads and writes the nodes that
.BR reac-pw (1)
publishes, and needs nothing else.
A control the box or the daemon cannot honour is shown with the reason instead
of a dead switch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the segments found, each box's badge and capability, and the asserted
values of each input, then exit.
No window is opened and nothing is written.
The exit status is 0 when at least one segment was found and 1 when none was.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REAC_STAGEBOXES_LOCALEDIR
Directory to read message catalogues from, instead of the build tree or the
installed location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reac-pw (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
